# 13. Metrics to freeze now for the final comparison

Do not wait until Step 4 to invent evaluation metrics.

Define them now.

At minimum, the final comparison should report separately:

### Code size

* executable representation LOC;
* representation/bridge theorem LOC;
* algorithm LOC;
* correctness proof LOC;
* time-analysis proof LOC;
* generic data-structure support LOC;
* graph-specific helper LOC.

### Logical/proof burden

* number of main invariants;
* number of representation invariants;
* number of bridge lemmas;
* number of new graph-specific lemmas;
* number of auxiliary generic lemmas;
* dependence on choice/noncomputability;
* theorem-statement complexity.

### Algorithmic result

* exact/concrete time bound;
* final asymptotic bound;
* preprocessing included or excluded;
* assumptions on primitive operations.

### Engineering burden

* build fragility;
* proof brittleness;
* heavy automation required;
* major failed implementation approaches;
* need for changes to the underlying graph foundation.

### Friction classification

For every significant difficulty, classify it as one of:

A. unavoidable Hierholzer/graph-theory complexity;
B. generic Lean/data-structure complexity;
C. graph-specification / representation friction;
D. missing graph-library API;
E. time-complexity framework friction.

The final comparison must not attribute category A/B/E difficulties to the graph library.

